{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_017aUeXsfC3Doqvi9Mkie8CP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Project State Summary\n\n**Problem**: This project derives formal specifications from Unix utility C source code, generates Go implementations from those specs using an AI coding agent (mage-claude-orchestrator), and verifies parity via differential testing against GNU reference binaries. The goal is to characterize where the methodology succeeds and fails.\n\n**Architecture**: Four-stage pipeline (extract → specify → synthesize → verify). Shared `pkg/` libraries (`testutils`, `sys`, `format`) support `cmd/<utility>/` packages. Each utility has a PRD, use case, and differential tests. `magefiles/` provides build infrastructure via cobbler-scaffold (excluded from generation).\n\n**Current State**:\n- Source code exists for `pkg/testutils/` (with tests), `pkg/sys/` (no tests), `pkg/format/` (no tests, issue #186 in progress)\n- No `cmd/` packages on the working branch\n- Spec complete for: wc, cat, sponge, du, ls, ts\n- Spec pending for: true, false, yes, basename, dirname, tee, head\n\n**Current Release**: rel00.0 (foundational infrastructure). `pkg/testutils` has code + tests. `pkg/format` has code + in-progress issue #186. `pkg/sys` has code but no tests. `magefiles` is excluded from generation (DD7).\n\n## Priority Reasoning\n\nPer P1 (release-driven priority), rel00.0 is the earliest incomplete release. Within rel00.0:\n- uc001-magefiles: excluded by DD7\n- uc002-format: in progress (#186)\n- uc004-testutils: code + tests exist (complete)\n- **uc003-sys: code exists, tests missing** — this is the gap\n\nPer P5 (libraries before consumers, test suites before feature code) and P2 (split implementation and tests), the sys implementation is done; the test task remains. This must complete before moving to rel01.0 (cmd/wc).\n\n```yaml\n- index: 0\n  title: \"Test pkg/sys terminal, stat, and signal operations (prd002-sys R1-R3)\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/product-requirements/prd002-sys.yaml (sys PRD with full requirements R1-R3)\n      - pkg/sys/terminal.go (TerminalWidth and IsTerminal implementations)\n      - pkg/sys/signal.go (InstallSIGPIPEHandler and OnTerminalResize implementations)\n      - pkg/sys/stat.go (Stat, Lstat, FileInfo struct, newFileInfo)\n      - pkg/sys/stat_linux.go (Linux fillFromStat with Mtim)\n      - pkg/sys/stat_darwin.go (Darwin fillFromStat with Mtimespec)\n      - pkg/testutils/difftest_test.go (project test patterns and conventions)\n\n    files:\n      - path: pkg/sys/terminal_test.go\n        action: create\n        note: Tests for TerminalWidth and IsTerminal\n      - path: pkg/sys/stat_test.go\n        action: create\n        note: Tests for Stat, Lstat, and FileInfo field population\n      - path: pkg/sys/signal_test.go\n        action: create\n        note: Tests for InstallSIGPIPEHandler and OnTerminalResize\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: \"Test terminal operations: TerminalWidth returns error for non-terminal fd (prd002-sys R1.1, R1.2) and IsTerminal returns false for pipe fd and true for terminal fd (prd002-sys R1.3)\"\n      - id: R2\n        text: \"Test SIGPIPE handler: InstallSIGPIPEHandler installs without panic and is safe to call multiple times (prd002-sys R1.5, R1.6)\"\n      - id: R3\n        text: \"Test file metadata: Stat and Lstat return correct FileInfo fields for regular files and symlinks, including Mode, Size, Nlink, Uid, Gid, Blocks, Blksize, and ModTime (prd002-sys R2.1, R2.2, R2.3)\"\n      - id: R4\n        text: \"Test terminal resize: OnTerminalResize registers a callback without error and the callback list is maintained across multiple registrations (prd002-sys R3.1, R3.2)\"\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: \"Test files mirror source file names per project convention: terminal_test.go, stat_test.go, signal_test.go\"\n      - id: D2\n        text: \"Platform-specific fillFromStat is tested indirectly through Stat and Lstat; build tags select the correct implementation per prd002-sys R2.3\"\n      - id: D3\n        text: \"Tests use package sys (not sys_test) for white-box access, following the pattern in pkg/testutils/difftest_test.go which uses package testutils\"\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: \"go test ./pkg/sys/... passes on the current platform\"\n      - id: AC2\n        text: \"Terminal tests verify TerminalWidth returns an error when fd is a pipe and IsTerminal returns false for a pipe file descriptor\"\n      - id: AC3\n        text: \"Stat tests verify all FileInfo fields (Mode, Size, Nlink, Uid, Gid, Dev, Ino, Blocks, Blksize, ModTime, Info) are populated correctly for a temporary file with known properties\"\n      - id: AC4\n        text: \"Lstat test creates a symlink and verifies FileInfo reflects the symlink itself, not the target\"\n      - id: AC5\n        text: \"Stat test with a nonexistent path returns a non-nil error\"\n      - id: AC6\n        text: \"Signal tests verify InstallSIGPIPEHandler and OnTerminalResize can be called without panic\"\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":28777,"cache_read_input_tokens":19289,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":28777},"output_tokens":10,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fcb5cf73-0b41-4ad9-942b-1b011e20f5ee","uuid":"6275a972-b060-49ef-ba00-7c734edea9ff"}
